
  THE DEPTH-WIDTH OBSTRUCTION

======================================================================

  I. DEPTH AND WIDTH IN THE OCF
  ----------------------------------------

  H = 1 + sum_{k>=1} 2^k * alpha_k

  DEPTH k: the size of the independent set.
    k=1: one cycle (depth 1)
    k=2: two disjoint cycles (depth 2)
    k=3: three mutually disjoint cycles (depth 3)

  WIDTH alpha_k: the number of independent sets at depth k.
    alpha_1 = total number of odd cycles
    alpha_2 = number of disjoint cycle PAIRS
    alpha_3 = number of disjoint cycle TRIPLES

  The 'weight' 2^k means: each unit of DEPTH doubles the contribution.
  Going one level deeper DOUBLES the payoff.
  But going deeper requires MORE VERTICES (disjoint cycles need room).

  THE OBSTRUCTION: at depth k, you need at least 3k vertices
  (k disjoint 3-cycles). So the maximum depth at n is floor(n/3).

  n    max depth    max 2^k     max H contribution from depth alone
  ------------------------------------------------------------
    3      1               2
    4      1               2
    5      1               2
    6      2               4
    7      2               4
    8      2               4
    9      3               8
   10      3               8
   11      3               8
   12      4              16
   13      4              16
   14      4              16
   15      5              32


  II. THE EVEN GRAPH CONNECTION
  ----------------------------------------

  A tournament on n vertices IS an orientation of the complete
  graph K_n. Every vertex has out-degree + in-degree = n-1.

  For odd n: every vertex has even total degree n-1.
  The UNDERLYING undirected graph (ignoring orientation)
  is K_n, which has degree n-1 = even for odd n.
  So for odd n: the tournament IS an even graph.

  For even n: degree n-1 is odd. NOT an even graph.
  But the COMPLEMENT (undirected K_n minus the tournament edges)
  is also NOT even.

  The key: a tournament on odd n vertices is an orientation of
  an EULERIAN graph (every vertex has even degree => Euler circuit).
  K_n for odd n has an Euler circuit.
  The tournament is a way to ORIENT this Euler circuit.

  Euler circuits visit every EDGE. Hamiltonian paths visit every VERTEX.
  The tournament lives at the intersection of these two worlds.


